---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Papers from '../components/Papers.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'ProfilePage',
  '@id': 'https://www.cody-peterson.com/#profilepage',
  mainEntity: { '@id': 'https://www.cody-peterson.com/#person' },
  dateModified: '2026-09-05',
  significantLink: ['https://www.cody-peterson.com/research/', 'https://www.cody-peterson.com/book/', 'https://www.seba.health/', 'https://logoi.health/'],
};
---
<Base title="Cody Peterson" seoTitle="Cody Peterson | Homer, Depth Psychology & AI-Assisted Research" description="Cody Peterson is a writer and depth psychology researcher. Homeric language, the history of feeling, AI-assisted research, and Seba.Health." jsonLd={jsonLd} noSuffix>
  <section class="inquiry-hero" aria-labelledby="inquiry-title">
    <div class="inquiry-hero-inner">
      <div class="inquiry-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Cody Peterson · Writer &amp; researcher</p>
        <h1 id="inquiry-title">The life<br />of <em>the soul.</em></h1>
        <p class="inquiry-deck">Homeric language.<br />Archetypal psychology.<br />New instruments of inquiry.</p>
        <p class="inquiry-introduction">I study what inherited language preserves of feeling and the formation of value—and what it asks of depth psychology today.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/research/">Enter the research <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#connections">How it connects <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <figure class="inquiry-hero-image">
        <img src="/images/life/canyon-silhouette.jpg" alt="Cody descending through the sandstone walls of a slot canyon" width="1200" height="1600" fetchpriority="high" />
        <figcaption><span>In the field, in another sense.</span><span>Fat Man’s Misery · Zion</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <nav class="inquiry-index" aria-label="Explore this page"><a href="#connections"><span>01</span> The inquiry</a><a href="#tools"><span>02</span> The tools</a><a href="#writing"><span>03</span> The writing</a><a href="#life"><span>04</span> The life</a></nav>
  </section>

  <section class="section paper-section" id="connections" aria-labelledby="connections-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="connection-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 · The connecting question</span><h2 id="connections-title">What does a life<br /><em>carry forward?</em></h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Recovery brought me back to books. Jung and Hillman deepened the questions. Homer brought me to an older language of feeling, endurance, and the soul.</p><p>Today, I design AI-assisted research programmes to follow these questions across texts and traditions. Seba and Logoi grow out of the same commitment: making the sources easier to reach, and the arguments open to examination.</p></div></div>
      <div class="inquiry-focus"><div><span class="eyebrow">Current focus · Homer &amp; depth psychology</span><h3>Who—or what—<em>has endured?</em></h3></div><div class="prose"><p>In <em>Odyssey</em> 20.17–23, Odysseus addresses his heart and recalls what it has already endured. My research asks how grammar distributes feeling and agency—and what later translations and psychological readings do with those relations.</p><p>The larger question is what this language can contribute to archetypal psychology’s understanding of feeling and value.</p><a class="text-link" href="/research/">Read the questions &amp; method <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="tools" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <header class="section-header section-heading-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 · Research &amp; public tools</span><h2 id="tools-title">Ways into <em>the work.</em></h2></div><p class="section-heading-note">A research practice, a philological workbench,<br />and a place to find the people behind the tradition.</p></header>
      <div class="tool-pair">
        <article class="tool-feature"><div class="tool-topline"><span class="eyebrow">Depth psychology · Community &amp; resources</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><h3><a href="https://www.seba.health/">Seba.Health</a></h3><p>Seba began with a practical question: how do you find a Jungian analyst? I built a directory, then a wider platform for exploring depth-psychology literature, ideas, and AI-assisted reflection.</p><p class="tool-detail">Operated on a not-for-profit basis. The directory, research resources, and Sebastian’s AI conversations serve different purposes.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.seba.health/">Explore Seba <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
        <article class="tool-feature"><div class="tool-topline"><span class="eyebrow">Philology · Texts &amp; evidence</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><h3><a href="https://logoi.health/">Logoi</a></h3><p>A workbench for reading texts, searching corpora, studying words, comparing versions, and examining usage. Built to keep the edition and passage within reach of the interpretation.</p><p class="tool-detail">One part of a broader practice of designing research programmes around questions that cross disciplines.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://logoi.health/">Open the workbench <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
      </div>
      <div class="method-note"><span class="eyebrow">Where AI fits</span><div><p>I use AI in source discovery, software, research organization, and testing interpretations. Generated output is provisional working material. The evidence comes from the sources; the judgments and arguments are my responsibility.</p><a class="text-link" href="/research/#method">Read my approach to AI &amp; evidence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="writing" class="section section-alt" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <header class="section-header section-heading-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 · Selected writing</span><h2 id="writing-title">From recovery<br /><em>to the ancient soul.</em></h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/research/#publications">Publication record <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></header>
      <div class="writing-layout"><article class="featured-book"><a href="/book/" class="book-cover-link" aria-label="Read about The Shadow of a Figure of Light"><img src="/images/book-cover.jpg" alt="The Shadow of a Figure of Light by Cody Peterson, book cover" width="400" height="600" loading="lazy" /></a><div><p class="work-status">Chiron Publications · 2024</p><h3><a href="/book/">The Shadow of <em>a Figure of Light</em></a></h3><p class="book-subtitle">The Archetype of the Alcoholic and the Journey to Enlightenment</p><p>Jung, Bill Wilson, and the Twelve Steps: an inquiry into the thirst for wholeness, written from within recovery.</p><a class="text-link" href="/book/">About the book &amp; signed copies <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><Papers /></div>
      <blockquote class="book-endorsement"><p>“It rests on the solid foundations of careful scholarship and personal experience.”</p><cite>Murray Stein · on <em>The Shadow of a Figure of Light</em></cite></blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="life" class="section" aria-labelledby="life-title"><div class="section-inner life-layout"><figure class="life-image"><img src="/images/life/narrows-laugh.jpg" alt="Cody laughing in a river canyon" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy" /><figcaption class="image-note">The good part.</figcaption></figure><div class="prose life-copy"><span class="eyebrow">04 · A life behind the work</span><h2 id="life-title">A scholar.<br />A builder.<br /><em>A trickster.</em></h2><p>I got sober on a curb in Las Vegas on March 4, 2013. The writing, the research, the businesses, and the return to school all belong to the life that followed.</p><p>I study psychology at the University of Utah and have been accepted to a master’s programme at Adams State University, beginning January 2027. Between the old texts and the things I build, I find my way back to the canyons of southern Utah.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">Read the full story <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section>

  <section class="conversation-band" aria-labelledby="conversation-title"><div class="section-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow">Continuing the conversation</span><h2 id="conversation-title">Ideas are better <em>in company.</em></h2><p>For research correspondence, seminars, and speaking invitations.</p><a class="text-link" href="mailto:cody@seba.health">cody@seba.health <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><nav aria-label="Talks and interviews"><a href="/videos/"><span>Lecture &amp; workshop archive</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/media/"><span>Interviews &amp; podcasts</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></nav></div></section>
</Base>
